The City of Cocoa Beach is committed to maintaining public spaces that enhance community engagement, preserve public welfare, and ensure high-quality amenities for residents and visitors. As part of this commitment, the City owns and operates Centennial Square and the Community Room, located at the City Hall Facility, which serve as vital venues for public gatherings, civic events, and non-commercial community activities.
To promote orderly and equitable access to these spaces, the City Commission finds it necessary to formally adopt a fee schedule that balances affordability for residents with the need to support ongoing maintenance, operations, and improvements. This resolution sets forth usage fees that reflect the value of these facilities while ensuring responsible use aligned with the City’s goals for health, safety, and quality of life.
This action will:
Provide a structured rental process for both residents and non-residents;
Establish reasonable usage fees that help sustain the public space without overburdening taxpayers;
Support the ongoing upkeep and functionality of Centennial Square and the Community Room;
Clarify expectations for users and enhance transparency in the City’s operations.
The proposed resolution will take effect immediately upon adoption by the Cocoa Beach City Commission at a regularly scheduled public meeting in 2025, with implementation carried out by City staff under the direction of the City Manager.
